<template>
    <heading>SelectProject async work</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>SelectProject</li>
        <li>async</li>
        <li>directory picker</li>
        <li>completion command</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p><code>selectProjectAndDispatch</code> is nested inside the <code>SelectProject</code> generator by a bundle reference. The generator starts it during priming, before yielding, so <code>showDirectoryPicker()</code> runs during the Select button's user activation.</p>
        <p>The async function awaits the picker and converts its outcome into one command: <code>ProjectDirectoryPicked</code> carries the directory handle; <code>ProjectPickerAborted</code> and <code>ProjectPickerFailed</code> carry the error. <code>AbortError</code> can mean dismissal, a restricted directory, or permission refusal.</p>
        <p>Completion dispatch is queued so the generator is suspended and installed on the handler stack before it receives the command, even when calling an unavailable picker throws before reaching <code>await</code>. Dispatch runs outside the picker error handler so an error in command handling is not classified as a picker failure.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>SelectProject async work</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
async function selectProjectAndDispatch() {
    let command;
    try {
        const directoryHandle = await window.showDirectoryPicker();
        command = { name: "ProjectDirectoryPicked", directoryHandle };
    } catch (error) {
        command = {
            name: error.name === "AbortError"
                ? "ProjectPickerAborted"
                : "ProjectPickerFailed",
            error
        };
    }

    // Also defer completion when the API is unavailable and the call throws.
    queueMicrotask(() => controller.dispatch(command));
}
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
